Version: [current]
Command: monochange

monochange discovers packages across Cargo, npm/pnpm/Bun, Deno, Dart/Flutter, Python, and Go, then coordinates version bumps, changelogs, and release automation from a single monochange.toml config.

[1m[97mUsage:[0m [93mmonochange[0m [95m[OPTIONS][0m [95m<COMMAND>[0m

[1m[96mRelease Commands:[0m
  [93mnext[0m           Show the next version for each release group and package without writing files
  [93mcreate[0m         Create a changeset file for one or more packages
  [93mpreview[0m        Preview planned version bumps, changelogs, and release artifacts without writing files
  [93mprepare[0m        Prepare version bumps, changelogs, and release artifacts
  [93mpublish[0m        Publish packages and inspect registry publishing state
  [93maffected[0m       Evaluate affected packages and changeset coverage
  [93mdiagnose[0m       Inspect changeset provenance and review metadata

[1m[96mWorkspace Commands:[0m
  [93minit[0m           Generate monochange.toml with detected packages and groups
  [93mpopulate[0m       Check for default CLI workflow aliases (none are provided in this version)
  [93mdiscover[0m       Discover packages across supported ecosystems
  [93mconfig[0m         Render resolved monochange configuration and workspace metadata
  [93mcheck[0m          Validate configuration, changesets, and run manifest lint rules
  [93mversions[0m       List package and group versions or sync internal dependency constraints
  [93mlint[0m           Inspect and scaffold manifest lint rules
  [93mmigrate[0m        Audit or migrate release metadata for monochange repositories

[1m[96mChange Analysis Commands:[0m
  [93mchange[0m         Determine the release severity of repository changes
  [93mchangeset[0m      Inspect and validate pending changeset intent
  [93mapi[0m            Inspect lower-level API diffs
  [93manalyze[0m        Analyze semantic changes for one package across main, head, and optional release baselines
  [93mnotes[0m          Render one configured release-note output without modifying release files

[1m[96mAutomation Commands:[0m
  [93mrun[0m            Run workflow commands defined in monochange.toml
  [93mstep[0m           Run built-in release workflow steps
  [93mcommand[0m        Open an interactive dashboard for adding or editing config-defined CLI commands
  [93mmcp[0m            Start the monochange MCP (Model Context Protocol) server over stdin/stdout
  [93mskill[0m          Read or install the bundled monochange agent skill
  [93msubagents[0m      Generate repo-local monochange subagents and agent guidance files
  [93msnapshot[0m       Print a normalized JSON snapshot of the CLI surface
  [93mhelp[0m           Show detailed help for a command

[1m[96mWorkflow Commands (monochange.toml):[0m
  [93mchange[0m         Create a change file for one or more packages (run it with `monochange run change`)
  [93mpublish-check[0m  Validate the release and preview package publishing in dry-run mode
  [93mrelease[0m        Prepare a pull request release from discovered change files. It should only be run in a github action.

